<title>USA: TABLE - Monterey Homes Corp Q2 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Monterey Homes Corp Q2 results.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>MONTEREY HOMES CORP. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			  Operating Results and Data (a)</p>
<p>					    Quarter Ended June 30,</p>
<p>					1997	   1996	    1996</p>
<p>				 Actual    Historical(b) Pro Forma(c)</p>
<p>Operating Results</p>
<p> Net income		  $1,958,068   $148,655 $1,331,704</p>
<p>Primary shares</p>
<p>  Per-share income(d)	  0.42	 0.04	0.29</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>			   (d)  4,657,723  3,317,298  4,657,723</p>
<p>Six Months</p>
<p>			     1997	   1996	    1996</p>
<p>				 Actual    Historical(b) Pro Forma(c)</p>
<p>Operating Results</p>
<p> Net income			$2,246,406   $232,988 $1,600,097</p>
<p>Primary shares</p>
<p>  Per-share income(c)		   0.48	 0.07	0.34</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding  (d)  4,664,448  3,295,208 4,664,448</p>
<p>(a)  Operating results and data do not include those of Legacy</p>
<p>Homes, as the acquisition did not become effective until</p>
<p>July 1, 1997. (b)  The historical amounts do not reflect any of Monterey</p>
<p>Homes' operations for 1996, as the merger between Homeplex</p>
<p>Mortgage Investments Corp. and Monterey Homes occurred</p>
<p>on Dec. 31, 1996. (c)  The pro forma amounts reflect the operating results as if</p>
<p>the merger of Homeplex Mortgage Investments Corp. with</p>
<p>Monterey Homes had occurred at the beginning of 1996. (d) Adjusted for a one-for-three reverse stock split which</p>
<p>occurred on Dec. 31, 1996.</p>
</text>
